(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the historical genesis of electrical engineering from Alessandro Volta's chemical cell to Michael Faraday's law of electromagnetic induction.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Historical Genesis of Electrical Engineering:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. The Advent of Continuous Current \(Alessandro Volta, 1800\):) Tj
T*
(   Before 1800, electricity was restricted to transient static electrostatic phenomena \(e.g.,) Tj
T*
(   Leyden jars and frictional generators\). Alessandro Volta invented the 'Voltaic Pile', stacking) Tj
T*
(   alternating discs of zinc and copper separated by brine-soaked cloth. This generated the) Tj
T*
(   world's first continuous direct current \(DC\), enabling systematic experimentation in) Tj
T*
(   electrochemistry, electromagnetism, and telegraphy.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Electromagnetic Interaction \(Hans Christian Oersted, 1820 & Andre-Marie Ampere, 1826\):) Tj
T*
(   Oersted observed that an electric current deflects a magnetic compass needle, proving that) Tj
T*
(   electric currents generate magnetic fields. Ampere formalized this mathematically, deriving) Tj
T*
(   Ampere's Circuital Law:) Tj
T*
(   $$\\oint \\mathbf{B} \\cdot d\\mathbf{l} = \\mu_0 I_{enc}$$) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Electromagnetic Induction \(Michael Faraday, 1831\):) Tj
T*
(   Faraday discovered the inverse effect: a dynamic, time-varying magnetic flux induces an) Tj
T*
(   electromotive force \(EMF\) in a closed conductive circuit:) Tj
T*
(   $$e = -\\frac{d\\Phi_B}{dt}$$) Tj
T*
(   The negative sign, formalized by Heinrich Lenz, reflects energy conservation. Faraday) Tj
T*
(   constructed the first rotating electromagnetic generator \(Faraday's Disc\) and demonstrated) Tj
T*
(   mutual induction between coupled coils, laying the foundational science for every modern power) Tj
T*
(   generator, alternator, and transformer.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
