(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the mathematical formulation of 3-phase AC power systems, detailing the derivation of line versus phase relationships in Star and Delta configurations.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Polyphase AC Power Formulation:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   A balanced 3-phase voltage source consists of three sinusoidal voltages of identical amplitude) Tj
T*
(   $V_m$ and angular frequency $\\omega$, mutually displaced by $120^\\circ$ \($2\\pi/3$ radians\):) Tj
T*
(   $$v_R\(t\) = V_m \\sin\(\\omega t\)$$) Tj
T*
(   $$v_Y\(t\) = V_m \\sin\(\\omega t - 120^\\circ\)$$) Tj
T*
(   $$v_B\(t\) = V_m \\sin\(\\omega t - 240^\\circ\) = V_m \\sin\(\\omega t + 120^\\circ\)$$) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Star \(Y\) Connection Derivation:) Tj
T*
(   - Line-to-Neutral \(Phase\) Voltages: $\\mathbf{V}_{RN} = V_{ph} \\angle 0^\\circ$, $\\mathbf{V}_{YN}) Tj
T*
(   = V_{ph} \\angle -120^\\circ$, $\\mathbf{V}_{BN} = V_{ph} \\angle 120^\\circ$.) Tj
T*
(   - Line-to-Line Voltage: $\\mathbf{V}_{RY} = \\mathbf{V}_{RN} - \\mathbf{V}_{YN} = V_{ph} - V_{ph}) Tj
T*
(   \(\\cos\(-120^\\circ\) + j \\sin\(-120^\\circ\)\)$.) Tj
T*
(   $$\\mathbf{V}_{RY} = V_{ph} - V_{ph} \\left\( -\\frac{1}{2} - j \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\right\) = V_{ph}) Tj
T*
(   \\left\( \\frac{3}{2} + j \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\right\) = \\sqrt{3} V_{ph} \\angle 30^\\circ$$) Tj
T*
(   Hence: $V_L = \\sqrt{3} V_{ph}$ and line current is identical to phase current: $I_L = I_{ph}$.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Delta \($\\Delta$\) Connection Derivation:) Tj
T*
(   - Line voltage equals phase voltage: $V_L = V_{ph}$.) Tj
T*
(   - Line current is phasor difference of phase currents: $\\mathbf{I}_R = \\mathbf{I}_{RY} -) Tj
T*
(   \\mathbf{I}_{BR} = \\sqrt{3} I_{ph} \\angle -30^\\circ$.) Tj
T*
(   Hence: $I_L = \\sqrt{3} I_{ph}$.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Total 3-Phase Active Power:) Tj
T*
(   In both configurations, total instantaneous active power is constant and independent of time:) Tj
T*
(   $$P_{3\\phi} = 3 V_{ph} I_{ph} \\cos\\theta = \\sqrt{3} V_L I_L \\cos\\theta$$) Tj
T*
(   Constant power flow eliminates torque pulsations in rotating machines, giving 3-phase machinery) Tj
T*
(   superior efficiency and vibration-free operation compared to single-phase equivalents.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
