(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the core pillars of Electrical Engineering curricula: Circuits, Machines, Power Systems, Power Electronics, and Control.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Core Pillars of Undergraduate Electrical Engineering:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Electric Circuits and Electromagnetic Fields:) Tj
T*
(   Forms the theoretical foundation. Covers Kirchhoff's laws, network theorems \(Thevenin, Norton,) Tj
T*
(   Superposition\), AC phasor analysis, frequency response, Laplace transforms, Maxwell's field) Tj
T*
(   equations, wave propagation, and boundary value problems.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Electrical Machines & Electromechanics:) Tj
T*
(   Studies magnetic circuits, transformers, DC machines \(generators/motors\), synchronous) Tj
T*
(   alternators, and 3-phase induction motors. Emphasizes equivalent circuits, torque-speed curves,) Tj
T*
