12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the physical origin, mathematical modeling, and operational mitigation of the Ferranti Effect in long EHV transmission lines.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Ferranti Effect in Long EHV Transmission Lines:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Phenomenon Description:) Tj
T*
(   Discovered by Sebastian Ziani de Ferranti in 1887, the Ferranti Effect describes the condition) Tj
T*
(   where the receiving-end voltage $V_R$ exceeds the sending-end voltage $V_S$ under no-load or) Tj
T*
(   lightly loaded conditions on long high-voltage overhead transmission lines or underground) Tj
T*
(   cables.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Modeling using Nominal-$\\pi$ Circuit:) Tj
T*
(   Let a line have series impedance $Z = R + j \\omega L$ and total shunt admittance $Y = j \\omega) Tj
T*
(   C$.) Tj
T*
(   Under open-circuit conditions \($I_R = 0$\):) Tj
T*
(   $$V_S = V_R \\left\( 1 + \\frac{Y Z}{2} \\right\)$$) Tj
T*
(   Substituting $Z \\approx j \\omega L$ and $Y = j \\omega C$ \(neglecting small series resistance) Tj
T*
(   $R$\):) Tj
T*
(   $$V_S = V_R \\left\( 1 + \\frac{\(j \\omega C\)\(j \\omega L\)}{2} \\right\) = V_R \\left\( 1 -) Tj
T*
(   \\frac{\\omega^2 L C}{2} \\right\)$$) Tj
T*
(   Rearranging reveals the voltage amplification ratio:) Tj
T*
(   $$V_R = \\frac{V_S}{1 - \\frac{\\omega^2 L C}{2}} > V_S$$) Tj
T*
(   Since $\\omega^2 L C > 0$, the denominator is strictly less than 1, proving $V_R > V_S$.) Tj
T*
ET

