() Tj
T*
(   3. Physical Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   The distributed line capacitance draws a continuous capacitive charging current $I_C = j \\omega) Tj
T*
(   C V$. This current leads the voltage by $90^\\circ$. When flowing through the line series) Tj
T*
(   inductive reactance $X_L$, it creates an inductive voltage drop $j I_C X_L = j \(j \\omega C V\)) Tj
T*
(   \(\\omega L\) = -\\omega^2 L C V$, which is $180^\\circ$ out of phase with the inductive drop of) Tj
T*
(   lagging current, effectively adding in-phase to the sending voltage.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Operational Hazards & Mitigation:) Tj
T*
(   Overvoltage degrades transformer insulation, saturates magnetic cores, and causes dielectric) Tj
T*
(   breakdown of switchgear. Mitigation is accomplished by connecting Shunt Reactors \(large) Tj
T*
(   air-core or gapped-iron inductors\) at line terminals and intermediate switching substations to) Tj
T*
(   absorb capacitive vars.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
