(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   High-Voltage Circuit Breakers:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. $SF_6$ Gas Circuit Breakers:) Tj
T*
(   - Arc Quenching Medium: Sulfur hexafluoride \($SF_6$\) is an electronegative gas possessing) Tj
T*
(   exceptional dielectric strength \(roughly 2.5 to 3 times that of air at 1 atm\) and high thermal) Tj
T*
(   conductivity.) Tj
T*
(   - Arc Extinction Process: When contacts part, the intense electric arc decomposes $SF_6$ into) Tj
T*
(   lower fluorides. Due to high electronegativity, $SF_6$ molecules rapidly capture free) Tj
T*
(   electrons, forming heavy, immobile negative ions, removing conductive carriers and building) Tj
T*
(   dielectric recovery strength across the contact gap in microseconds.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Vacuum Circuit Breakers \(VCB\):) Tj
T*
(   - Arc Quenching Medium: High vacuum \($< 10^{-6}$ torr\). At this pressure, the mean free path of) Tj
T*
(   residual gas molecules exceeds contact clearance dimensions.) Tj
T*
(   - Arc Dynamics: The arc consists entirely of ionized metal vapor liberated from the contact) Tj
T*
(   surfaces. At current zero, the metal vapor expands and condenses onto surrounding metallic) Tj
T*
(   condensation shields within microseconds, restoring dielectric strength almost instantaneously.) Tj
T*
(   VCBs are standard for medium-voltage switchgear \(11 kV to 33 kV\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
