12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Formulate the symmetrical component transformation and explain its utility in analyzing unbalanced grid faults.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Symmetrical Components Method \(Fortescue Theorem, 1918\):) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Any unbalanced set of three-phase phasors can be resolved into three balanced symmetrical) Tj
T*
(   components:) Tj
T*
(   $$\\begin{bmatrix} \\mathbf{V}_a \\\\ \\mathbf{V}_b \\\\ \\mathbf{V}_c \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}) Tj
T*
(   1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & a^2 & a \\\\ 1 & a & a^2 \\end{bmatrix} \\begin{bmatrix} \\mathbf{V}_{a0} \\\\) Tj
T*
(   \\mathbf{V}_{a1} \\\\ \\mathbf{V}_{a2} \\end{bmatrix}$$) Tj
T*
(   where $a = 1 \\angle 120^\\circ = -\\frac{1}{2} + j \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ is the complex phase-shift) Tj
T*
(   operator.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   - Positive Sequence \($V_{a1}$\): Balanced phasors with identical magnitude, phase sequence ABC.) Tj
T*
(   - Negative Sequence \($V_{a2}$\): Balanced phasors with sequence ACB, indicating unbalance and) Tj
T*
(   producing reverse rotating fields in machines.) Tj
T*
(   - Zero Sequence \($V_{a0}$\): Three phasors of equal magnitude and identical phase angle,) Tj
T*
(   indicating ground return currents.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
