(   Substation Grounding Grid Design \(IEEE Std 80\):) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Safety Objectives:) Tj
T*
(   During a ground fault, large fault currents enter the earth, creating potential gradients along) Tj
T*
(   the ground surface. The grounding grid ensures safety limits for:) Tj
T*
(   - Step Potential \($E_{step}$\): Potential difference between a person's feet spaced 1 meter) Tj
T*
(   apart without touching any grounded structure.) Tj
T*
(   - Touch Potential \($E_{touch}$\): Potential difference between a person's hand touching a) Tj
T*
(   grounded structure and their feet 1 meter away.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Tolerable Body Voltage Limits:) Tj
T*
(   $$E_{touch} = \\frac{1000 + 1.5 C_s \\rho_s}{\\sqrt{t_s}} \\cdot 0.116$$) Tj
T*
(   Grounding meshes of buried copper conductors and vertical ground rods are engineered to reduce) Tj
T*
(   mesh resistance $R_g$ below 1 Ohm and keep touch voltages below human ventricular fibrillation) Tj
T*
(   thresholds.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
