(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the IEEE Code of Ethics and its fundamental ethical obligations for practicing electrical engineers.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   IEEE Code of Ethics Commitments:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Electrical engineers are entrusted with designing critical national infrastructure,) Tj
T*
(   communications, and power grids.) Tj
T*
(   Core Tenets:) Tj
T*
(   1. Public Safety & Welfare: Hold paramount the safety, health, and welfare of the public and) Tj
T*
(   the environment, disclosing factors that might endanger the public.) Tj
T*
(   2. Professional Integrity: Avoid unlawful conduct, conflicts of interest, and bribery, treating) Tj
T*
(   all persons fairly and respectfully.) Tj
T*
(   3. Technical Honesty: State claims and estimates truthfully based on available engineering data) Tj
T*
(   and acknowledge engineering errors promptly.) Tj
T*
(   4. Continuous Competence: Maintain professional competence, undertake technological tasks only) Tj
T*
(   if qualified by training or experience, and mentor the next generation of engineers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
