(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the construction and operation of a Synchronous Condenser for grid voltage support and inertia.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Synchronous Condensers in Modern Grids:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   A synchronous condenser is a synchronous machine operating without a mechanical load or prime) Tj
T*
(   mover.) Tj
T*
(   - Overexcited Mode: Operates at leading power factor, supplying reactive power \(capacitive) Tj
T*
(   vars\) to boost grid voltage.) Tj
T*
(   - Underexcited Mode: Operates at lagging power factor, absorbing reactive power \(inductive) Tj
T*
(   vars\) to prevent overvoltages.) Tj
T*
(   - Physical Inertia: Because it has a massive rotating rotor, it inherently injects genuine) Tj
T*
(   physical rotational inertia into the grid, stabilizing frequency in renewable-rich grids.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
