BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the torque-speed equation for a 3-phase induction motor and explain the maximum torque condition.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Induction Motor Torque Derivation:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   From the per-phase equivalent circuit, developed electromagnetic torque is:) Tj
T*
(   $$T = \\frac{3}{\\omega_s} \\cdot \\frac{V_1^2 \\cdot \(R_2' / s\)}{\(R_1 + R_2' / s\)^2 + \(X_1 +) Tj
T*
(   X_2'\)^2}$$) Tj
T*
(   Condition for Maximum \(Breakdown\) Torque:) Tj
T*
(   Differentiating $T$ with respect to slip $s$ and equating to zero:) Tj
T*
(   $$s_{max} = \\frac{R_2'}{\\sqrt{R_1^2 + \(X_1 + X_2'\)^2}}$$) Tj
T*
(   Maximum torque $T_{max} = \\frac{3 V_1^2}{2 \\omega_s [R_1 + \\sqrt{R_1^2 + \(X_1 + X_2'\)^2}]}$ is) Tj
T*
(   strictly independent of rotor resistance $R_2'$, although the slip at which it occurs is) Tj
T*
(   directly proportional to $R_2'$.) Tj
