(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the principles of Wide Area Monitoring Systems \(WAMS\) using Phasor Measurement Units \(PMUs\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Wide Area Monitoring Systems \(WAMS\):) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. PMU Operation: Phasor Measurement Units use GPS satellite signals to timestamp voltage and) Tj
T*
(   current phasors with 1-microsecond precision, sampling at 50-60 frames/sec.) Tj
T*
(   2. Real-Time Situational Awareness: Unlike SCADA which updates every 2-4 seconds without) Tj
T*
(   synchronized phase angles, WAMS allows operators to observe angular separations between distant) Tj
T*
(   regions in real-time, detecting inter-area electromechanical oscillations \(0.1 to 1 Hz\) and) Tj
T*
(   dynamic instability before blackouts occur.) Tj
