(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the causes and characteristics of Subsynchronous Resonance \(SSR\) in series-compensated power grids.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Subsynchronous Resonance \(SSR\):) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   When series capacitors are used to compensate transmission line inductance, the electrical) Tj
T*
(   circuit forms an LC resonant circuit with natural frequency below nominal grid frequency:) Tj
T*
(   $$f_{er} = f_0 \\sqrt{\\frac{X_C}{X_L}} < f_0$$) Tj
T*
(   This electrical frequency induces stator currents that interact with the rotor, creating slip) Tj
T*
(   frequency rotor currents. If this frequency matches one of the torsional mechanical natural) Tj
T*
(   resonance modes of the turbine-generator multi-mass shaft, violent mechanical oscillations) Tj
T*
(   build up, causing catastrophic shaft fatigue and shearing.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
