(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the principles of arc flash hazard analysis according to NFPA 70E and IEEE Std 1584.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Arc Flash Hazard Analysis:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Incident Energy \($E$\): The amount of thermal energy impressed on a surface at a specified) Tj
T*
(   working distance during an electrical arc fault, measured in $\\text{cal/cm}^2$.) Tj
T*
(   2. Flash Protection Boundary: Distance from exposed energized conductors where incident energy) Tj
T*
(   drops to $1.2 \\text{ cal/cm}^2$ \(threshold for second-degree burns\).) Tj
T*
(   3. PPE Categories: Ranging from Category 1 \($4 \\text{ cal/cm}^2$\) to Category 4 \($40 \\text{) Tj
T*
(   cal/cm}^2$\), mandating arc-rated face shields, flame-resistant suits, and insulating gloves.) Tj
T*
() Tj
