(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the harmonic distortion limits and Point of Common Coupling \(PCC\) in IEEE Std 519.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   IEEE Std 519 Harmonic Control:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Point of Common Coupling \(PCC\): The electrical boundary interface where the industrial) Tj
T*
(   consumer's facility connects to the public utility distribution network.) Tj
T*
(   2. Total Demand Distortion \(TDD\): Harmonic current distortion expressed as a percentage of) Tj
T*
(   maximum consumer load demand current.) Tj
T*
(   3. Voltage THD Limits: IEEE 519 specifies that for bus voltages $\\le 69$ kV, voltage THD must) Tj
T*
(   not exceed 5.0%, with individual harmonic voltage distortion capped at 3.0%, mandating harmonic) Tj
T*
(   filters for non-linear power converter loads.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
