(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the primary frequency control mechanisms in conventional thermal and hydro generating units.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Primary Frequency Control \(Droop Governor Mechanism\):) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Turbine governors operate on speed droop characteristic $R$ \(typically 4% to 5%\):) Tj
T*
(   $$R = \\frac{\\Delta f / f_0}{\\Delta P / P_{rated}} \\times 100\\%$$) Tj
T*
(   When grid frequency drops due to load increase, the droop governor automatically increases fuel) Tj
T*
(   or steam valve position proportionally to restore mechanical power. The droop characteristic) Tj
T*
(   ensures that multiple parallel generators share load changes stably according to their power) Tj
T*
(   ratings without fighting each other.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
