(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss the fundamental principles of engineering design, safety margins, and life-cycle assessment in electrical projects.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Engineering Design Principles & Life-Cycle Analysis:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Safety Factors & Redundancy: Electrical equipment must be sized with safety factors) Tj
T*
(   \(typically 1.25 to 1.5\) accounting for ambient thermal derating, prospective short-circuit) Tj
T*
(   currents, and insulation aging.) Tj
T*
(   2. Life-Cycle Assessment \(LCA\): Evaluates total environmental and financial impacts across all) Tj
T*
(   phases: raw material extraction \(copper, silicon, lithium\), manufacturing, 25-30 year) Tj
T*
(   operational maintenance, and end-of-life recycling.) Tj
T*
(   3. Sustainability: Modern electrical design mandates eco-design principles, minimizing SF6) Tj
T*
(   leakage, prioritizing biodegradable ester transformer oils, and implementing circular economy) Tj
T*
(   recycling for battery cells and solar panels.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
